{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The desirable ones.</b> They were desired from Nimrod, and they were desirable in that painted upon them were all the beasts and birds of the world, appearing as though alive; and when he was in the field, the beasts and birds would come to him and be caught of themselves. And to this midrash it is difficult: why did she dress Jacob in them? It appears that she wanted to make him entirely like Esau's likeness."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:08.528626864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}